        "problem": "Evaluate ${\\int }_{1}^{4}\u27e84t-1,\\sqrt{t}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t.$",
        "worked_solution": "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each componentt separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{4}\u27e84t-1,\\,\\sqrt{t}\u27e9\\,\\text{d}t & =\u27e8{\\int }_{1}^{4}(4t-1)\\,\\text{d}t,{\\int }_{1}^{4}\\sqrt{t}\\,\\text{d}t\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(2{t}^{2}-t){|}_{1}^{4},\\,(\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}){|}_{1}^{4}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e8(2(4)^{2}-4)-(2(1)^{2}-1),\\,\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{4}^{3}}-\\frac{2}{3}\\sqrt{{1}^{3}}\u27e9 \\\\  & =\u27e827,\\,\\frac{14}{3}\u27e9\\end{aligned}\n$$",
